# The fixes after step 23's review, its sessions part: a history read while
# a turn runs, and leaving a session part-way. Each rule broken alone.

[break] an-item-in-progress-at-the-read-is-skipped
rule: An item the read gives in progress is drawn as far as it had gone, and goes on with the events after the read.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::history_read
find:
    if incomplete {
        self.mapper.in_progress(&mut self.transcript, &item, now);
    } else {
replace:
    if incomplete {
    } else {
caught-by:
    app::tests::sessions::an_answer_in_progress_at_the_read_is_drawn_once_and_whole
    app::tests::sessions::a_command_running_at_the_read_ends_in_one_box_that_succeeded

[break] events-of-an-item-in-progress-are-dropped-after-the-read
rule: Of an item the read holds in progress, the events after the read's seq continue it; those up to it are in its content.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::history_read
find: Some(Some(seq)) => event.seq > *seq,
replace: Some(Some(_)) => false,
caught-by:
    app::tests::sessions::an_answer_in_progress_at_the_read_is_drawn_once_and_whole

[break] events-of-an-item-in-progress-are-all-shown
rule: Of an item the read holds in progress, the events up to the read's seq are dropped: its content holds them.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::history_read
find: Some(Some(seq)) => event.seq > *seq,
replace: Some(Some(_)) => true,
caught-by:
    app::tests::sessions::an_answer_in_progress_at_the_read_is_drawn_once_and_whole

[break] a-turn-is-running-from-the-open-alone
rule: Whether a turn ran at the read is taken from the turn's events held up to it, not only from what the open said.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::history_read
find: Event::TurnStarted(_) => running = true,
replace: Event::TurnStarted(_) => {}
caught-by:
    app::tests::sessions::a_call_of_a_turn_that_began_before_the_read_is_not_cut_off

[break] an-item-in-progress-does-not-say-a-turn-runs
